{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>כי</b> — its meaning is <b>הנה</b> [behold], as in 'for we are consumed in Your anger' — we are consumed like a <b>הגה</b> [utterance], as in 'and a הגה proceeds from his mouth' (Isaiah 11:4), for speech has no permanence: at the moment the speaker speaks it exists, and afterward it is as though it never was."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:46.138395791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}